# Performance & Minimal Code — phpupgrade

ElintPOS on **CI 3.1.13 / PHP 8.5**. Every change must stay **small, fast, and behavior-identical**.

## Performance Budget

| Target | Limit |
|--------|--------|
| Screen load (logged-in) | **< 1s** TTFB on local WAMP |
| AJAX / DataTables / product search | **< 1s** |
| Sale submit / save | **< 2s** acceptable (DB write); avoid extra work in same request |
| PDF generation | On-demand only — never on every page load |

If a fix risks slowing hot paths (POS, Sales list, login), **choose the smaller fix** or report to user.

## No Over-Engineering (Required)

**Do NOT add during upgrade unless user explicitly asks:**

- New service layers, repositories, DTOs, or base classes
- Generic helpers used once
- Caching (Redis, file cache, memo wrappers)
- New Composer packages for “cleaner” code
- Refactors “while we’re here” (rename, reorder, extract method)
- Extra test scripts outside `upgrade/` directory (keep new `phase4_*` scripts in `upgrade/`)
- `#[\AllowDynamicProperties]` on every class when parent already has it
- Wrapping 1-line null guards in new functions

**DO:**

- Fix only the failing line/path (PHP 8.5 fatal, null, type)
- Reuse existing CI patterns: `$this->db->where()`, `$this->data`, `form_open()`
- One guard, one query pattern — match surrounding code

```php
// ❌ Over-engineered
class SaleDepositLogHelper {
    public static function isNonEmpty($log) { return is_array($log) && count($log) > 0; }
}

// ✅ Minimal (same behavior)
$depositLog = array();
// ...
if (!empty($depositLog)) { ... }
```

## Before You Edit — Quick Check

1. **Queries**: No new query inside loops; no duplicate `getSetting()` / `getUser()` per row.
2. **Views**: No DB calls added to views; no `foreach` on unbounded result without limit.
3. **Controllers**: No loading MPDF/Stripe/Google SDK unless that action needs it.
4. **Autoload**: Don’t add libraries to global autoload for one screen.
5. **Diff size**: Prefer < 20 lines per file unless scan proves more are required.

## Hot Paths (extra care)

| Path | Keep fast |
|------|-----------|
| `Pos.php` / `Pos_elite.php` | `index`, `getProductDataByCode`, sale submit |
| `Sales.php` | list AJAX, add/edit save |
| `Auth.php` | login |
| `Welcome.php` | dashboard widgets |
| `sales/suggestions` | product autocomplete |

Avoid `sleep()`, remote HTTP, or heavy `file_get_contents` on these paths.

## Performance Verify (when touching hot paths)

After changes, run existing smoke tests — do not invent heavy suites:

```bash
c:\wamp64\bin\php\php8.5.0\php.exe upgrade\phase4_pos_test.php <user> <pass>
c:\wamp64\bin\php\php8.5.0\php.exe upgrade\phase4_pos_deep_test.php <user> <pass>
```

If no test exists for the module, one **HTTP 200 + no fatal** check is enough — don’t build frameworks.

## Conflicts with Upgrade Rules

| php-upgrade-core | This rule |
|------------------|-----------|
| Fix PHP 8.5 errors | Yes — minimal line fix only |
| No business logic change | Yes — performance fixes must not alter totals/workflows |
| Use subagents for module scans | Yes — but **implement** with smallest diff, not broad refactors |

When in doubt: **smallest correct fix that keeps the screen under 1 second.**
